{"step_index":635,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-14T04:43:41Z","content":"### Why the Error Happened:\nThe server failed to start because another Java process (the previous server instance) was already running and listening on **port 8080**. When a second instance tried to bind to port 8080, Spring Boot threw `Web server failed to start. Port 8080 was already in use.`\n\n---\n\n### What Was Done to Fix It:\n\n1. **Freed Port 8080**:\n   - The previous background Java process occupying port 8080 was identified and terminated. Port 8080 is now completely released.\n\n2. **Automated Port Cleanup in `run-app.bat`**:\n   - Updated `run-app.bat` to automatically check if port 8080 is in use before launching the server.\n   - If an old instance is still running, `run-app.bat` will now cleanly terminate that process first, preventing this error from occurring again.\n\n---\n\n### How to Run:\nYou can now run either:\n1. Double-click **`run-app.bat`** in the project folder; OR\n2. In PowerShell, execute:\n   ```powershell\n   .\\run-app.bat\n   ```\n\nThe application will start up cleanly on **`http://localhost:8080`**."}
